/*
 * THE SLOVAK NAME-DAY CALENDAR.
 * =============================
 *
 * Source: the Oficiálne kalendárium published by the Kalendárna komisia at the
 * Ministerstvo kultúry Slovenskej republiky - the body that actually sets the
 * Slovak calendar, which is what makes it a standard rather than one opinion
 * among many. Extracted from the ministry's published PDF by two independent
 * text-extraction passes that agreed on all 366 days.
 *
 * Cross-checked against independent captures. Where they disagree with the
 * ministry, the ministry is followed and the disagreement is recorded on the
 * record itself in `verificationNote`, so a later reader can see that a choice
 * was made rather than finding a bare date and having to trust it.
 *
 * ONE DELIBERATE DEPARTURE FROM THE SOURCE
 * 10 January. The ministry document prints "Daša" without the acute in both its
 * 2019 and 2025 editions; every independent source and ordinary Slovak usage
 * have "Dáša". A long-lived typo in a source is still a typo, and dropping a
 * diacritic from someone's name is the precise kind of small wrongness this
 * dataset exists to avoid. Recorded as `conflicting` with the reason attached.
 *
 * WHY EVERY DATE IS PRESENT, INCLUDING THE FOUR WITH NO NAME
 * 1 January, 1 May, 2 November and 25 December carry no personal name. They stay
 * in the dataset as empty records because the calendar's completeness is
 * enforced by test, and because "this day has no name day" is a real answer that
 * a gap in the data cannot express.
 */
